        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: கட்டில்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "கட்டில் (kaṭṭil) — \"a bed\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A bed — and in Tamil it is named as a made thing: a frame with cords or webbing tied across it."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "You already have தூக்கம் (tūkkam), sleep. The pair is easy to hold: the தூக்கம் happens on the கட்டில் (kaṭṭil)."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its middle is the doubled ட்ட you took apart in சட்டை, and it closes on ல் — a letter with the vowel taken off, exactly like the ண் in வண்டி, except that here there is nothing after it to lean on."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Two, and you can now name where you sleep."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
