          "title": "You'll want to know: சுவர்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சுவர் (suvar) — \"a wall\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The wall of a room or a house."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is short and it is bare — two letters and a closing ர், no vowel signs hanging off the front of anything. Words shaped this plainly are usually old ones, and this is one of them."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It is also the surface that makes உள்ளே and வெளியே mean anything: a சுவர் (suvar) is what there is an inside and an outside of."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three, and the room has an edge."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
