            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தரை (tarai) — \"the floor\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The floor — and also the ground outside. Tamil does not need two words for it; what is under your feet is தரை (tarai) wherever you are standing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This is where the கோலம் (kōlam) is drawn each morning, just inside the வாசல். Both of those words are already yours, and this is the one that was missing to put them in a place."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It ends in the ை again — the fifth word in three chapters to do so."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Four, and the room has a bottom."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
