              "text": "கூரை (kūrai) — \"a roof\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The roof over you."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "With தரை (tarai) under your feet and கூரை (kūrai) over your head, the room has both ends — and you already have the two words for the space between them: மேலே and கீழே. Point up at the கூரை (kūrai), down at the தரை (tarai), and every word in that sentence is one you have been taught."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its ூ is the long u sign, and it ends, like தரை (tarai), in ை."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Five: a table, a bed, a wall, a floor and a roof."
